{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"entry":1},{"title":2,"description":3,"version":4,"date":5,"html":6,"path":7},"Changelog, a light and dark switch, custom heroes and template updates","Four things the first version couldn't do.","0.2.0","10 NOV 2026","\u003Cp class=\"lead\">Sites can now keep release notes, readers can pick light or dark, a site can bring its own hero demo, and existing sites can pull in template improvements.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"changelog\">Changelog\u003Ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#changelog\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">\u003Csvg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"M6.5 9.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 0l2.2-2.2a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4-4l-.7.7\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M9.5 6.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4 0L3.3 8.7a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 4l.7-.7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Put dated Markdown files in \u003Ccode>content/changelog\u003C/code>, named like \u003Ccode>2026-11-10-what-changed.md\u003C/code>. The site adds a Changelog link to the header, an index page, a page per entry, Markdown copies and entries in \u003Ccode>llms.txt\u003C/code>. See \u003Ca href=\"/docs/changelog\">Changelog\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"light-and-dark\">Light and dark\u003Ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#light-and-dark\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">\u003Csvg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"M6.5 9.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 0l2.2-2.2a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4-4l-.7.7\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M9.5 6.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4 0L3.3 8.7a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 4l.7-.7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>There&#39;s now a switch in the header and the docs sidebar. Pages still follow the system until a reader picks, and the choice is remembered.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"custom-heroes\">Custom heroes\u003Ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#custom-heroes\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">\u003Csvg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"M6.5 9.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 0l2.2-2.2a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4-4l-.7.7\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M9.5 6.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4 0L3.3 8.7a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 4l.7-.7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Drop a \u003Ccode>Hero.svelte\u003C/code> into \u003Ccode>src/custom\u003C/code> and it replaces the sample on the landing page. CSS files there load on every page. Template updates never touch that folder.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"template-updates\">Template updates\u003Ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#template-updates\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">\u003Csvg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"M6.5 9.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 0l2.2-2.2a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4-4l-.7.7\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M9.5 6.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4 0L3.3 8.7a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 4l.7-.7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>scripts/update-site.sh\u003C/code> brings a site up to the latest template. It replaces the template&#39;s code and leaves your words, images and \u003Ccode>src/custom\u003C/code> alone. See \u003Ca href=\"/docs/updating\">Updating a site\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\n","/changelog/2026-11-10-first-release"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
